{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Data Integration.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Data Integration.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"data integration data integration","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Data Integration.md","fileName":"Data Integration.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Data Integration","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-09 00:00\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Cloud Integration and Messaging]] · [[Evidence-Based Data Decisions]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cloud Integration and Messaging","Evidence-Based Data Decisions","Common Data Model","cloudcomputing_mit.epub","frontiersofdatascience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Data Integration.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Data Integration.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"data integration data integration","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Data Integration.md","fileName":"Data Integration.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Data Integration","heading":"Data Integration","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Data integration allows applications or services to exchange and jointly use information. It requires both a compatible representation and a shared understanding of what the represented fields mean.\n\nTwo files can use the same format while containing incompatible data models, and two services can describe the same business concept in different formats. A [[Common Data Model]] plus agreed encodings and validation rules makes the exchange interpretable rather than merely transferable.\n\nIn an evidence pipeline, integration combines extracted records before cleaning, storage, and exploration. The join rules and entity matches determine which observations are treated as belonging together, so integration decisions become part of the evidence behind a conclusion.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cloud Integration and Messaging","Evidence-Based Data Decisions","Common Data Model","cloudcomputing_mit.epub","frontiersofdatascience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Data Integration.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Data Integration.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"data integration data integration","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Data Integration.md","fileName":"Data Integration.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Data Integration","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[cloudcomputing_mit.epub]]\n\n[[frontiersofdatascience.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cloud Integration and Messaging","Evidence-Based Data Decisions","Common Data Model","cloudcomputing_mit.epub","frontiersofdatascience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}